WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:07.823
IEC 61850 Explorer: connect to an IED, open an SCL file, or analyse a capture.
The demo: AA1 Northfield, a made-up substation in the repository.

2
00:00:07.823 --> 00:00:13.075
Open the substation’s SCD. It lists six IEDs; browse the transformer protection offline, no IED needed.

3
00:00:13.075 --> 00:00:18.303
Its model as the SCL defines it: logical devices, logical nodes, data objects and their functional constraints.

4
00:00:18.303 --> 00:00:24.161
Search by quantity: the IEC 61850 namespace knows which data objects measure Impedance, Active energy, Voltage…

5
00:00:24.161 --> 00:00:30.132
The namespace panel says what the selected node is: class, CDC, presence, and the quantity, phase and unit.

6
00:00:30.132 --> 00:00:36.266
Check conformance to the namespace. YLTC1 declares the vendor namespace CORVANE 7-4X:2026A, which is not loaded.

7
00:00:36.266 --> 00:00:43.043
Load the vendor’s NSD package and check again: its logical node and data objects are now checked against their definitions.

8
00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:51.022
Feeder 2’s CID is an Edition 1 file: its logical devices declare no namespace, so they are checked as Edition 1.

9
00:00:51.022 --> 00:00:56.958
Export the point list for SCADA or gateway engineering: every attribute with FC, CDC, type, quantity, data sets and reports.

10
00:00:56.958 --> 00:01:01.324
Now live. First open feeder 1’s CID, to compare with the IED later.

11
00:01:01.324 --> 00:01:09.186
Connect to feeder 1, served by make demo-ieds on 127.0.0.1:10201. The session starts in Observe mode: reads only.

12
00:01:09.186 --> 00:01:17.302
Read a data object: the value with its quality and time stamp, and the MMS domain and item it was read from.

13
00:01:17.302 --> 00:01:24.191
Watch points of any IED in one table and poll them; the measurements change every 2 s.

14
00:01:24.191 --> 00:01:30.119
A logical device shows its data sets, report control blocks, logs and setting groups. Read a data set in one request.

15
00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:33.614
Setting groups: the protection has two, group 1 is active.

16
00:01:33.614 --> 00:01:40.001
The IED’s files: its CID and the COMTRADE record of this morning’s fault, ready to download.

17
00:01:40.001 --> 00:01:44.995
Compare the IED with its CID, configured values included (FC CF, DC, SP, SG).

18
00:01:44.995 --> 00:01:51.440
Exactly two differences: someone updated the firmware (2.4.1) and set I> to 650 A on the front panel.

19
00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:58.453
Changes need Commission mode: a grant with a reason, a duration and capabilities (here reports and controls), on a second, restricted association.

20
00:01:58.453 --> 00:02:05.228
Subscribe to a report control block: the reports arrive with their reasons for inclusion.

21
00:02:05.228 --> 00:02:09.865
Open disconnector QB1 (SBO, enhanced security). You confirm before anything is sent.

22
00:02:09.865 --> 00:02:16.629
The IED refuses: blocked-by-interlocking, because breaker QA1 is still closed.

23
00:02:16.629 --> 00:02:21.146
Open breaker QA1 first: select, operate and the CommandTermination, each step shown.

24
00:02:21.146 --> 00:02:25.619
Operated: select, operate and the CommandTermination all ok. The position went from on to off.

25
00:02:25.619 --> 00:02:34.501
The audit trail records the grant, the subscription and every control, refused or not.
Revoke ends the grant and releases the report control block.

26
00:02:34.501 --> 00:02:40.125
Analyse a capture offline: the station fault at 09:00:10, with MMS, GOOSE and Sampled Values on one mirror port.

27
00:02:40.125 --> 00:02:47.057
Link it to feeder 1’s SCL model: MMS names become IEC 61850 references, and reports are decoded against their data sets.

28
00:02:47.057 --> 00:02:52.980
The timeline: every confirmed service with its status, latency and the objects it named.

29
00:02:52.980 --> 00:03:00.075
Feeder 1’s reports, decoded against dsTrip: starts, operate and trip, each with its reason;
the components named by the model: general, phsA…, the quality q, the time t.

30
00:03:00.075 --> 00:03:06.333
GOOSE: feeder 1’s trip, then the breaker failure 152 ms later. Sampled Values: 6000 frames, none lost.

31
00:03:06.333 --> 00:03:11.773
Capture 08: a bad morning on the station bus. Link it to feeder 2 and open the findings.

32
00:03:11.773 --> 00:03:19.716
A lost TCP segment, unanswered requests, a midstream association, a reject, GOOSE and SV losses: each with where and why.

33
00:03:19.716 --> 00:03:24.222
IEC 61850 Explorer by OT Fabric: inspect, commission, compare and analyse. MIT licensed.
